.TH std::any::reset 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::any::reset \- std::any::reset

.SH Synopsis
void reset() noexcept;  \fI(since C++17)\fP

If *this contains a value, destroys the contained value.

*this does not contain a value after this call.

.SH Parameters

\fI(none)\fP

.SH Return value

\fI(none)\fP

.SH Example


// Run this code

#include <any>
#include <cassert>

int main()
{
    std::any a{42};
    assert(a.has_value());
    a.reset();
    assert(not a.has_value());
}

.SH See also

has_value checks if object holds a value
          \fI(public member function)\fP
